<title>NETHERLANDS: Wolters issues convertible for employees.</title>
<headline>Wolters issues convertible for employees.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Business publisher Wolters Kluwer NV said on Monday it would issue a 10 million guilder subordinated convertible bond to its Dutch employees.</p>
<p>On November 29 of this year, the employees of the firm's Dutch subsidiaries can buy the bonds which carry a coupon of three percent and have a maturity of four years.</p>
<p>The bonds can be swapped for ordinary Wolters Kluwer shares at any time before the issue matures at a conversion price of 229 guilders per share. If all bonds are converted, this will raise the number of outstanding shares by about 44,000, Wolters said. It now has about 68.5 million shares outstanding.</p>
</text>
